    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "The v2 config, the skip-on-missing Go branch in the existing hook style and the AGENTS.md row are all present, but .golangci.yml never enables lll at line-length 100, so golangci-width-100 fails and correctness is capped at 4; the hook also lints and format-checks the whole module rather than gofmt-checking only the staged Go files."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Only .golangci.yml, scripts/lint-staged.sh and AGENTS.md changed: no workflow was added, Go sources and other languages' configs and opt-outs were untouched, and the only extras are a few additional linters in the new config."
      },
      {
        "name": "explanation",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "The reply explains that no CI lint job was added because tests.yml only runs go test, and it lists what was run and what could not be verified (config verify was blocked), but it never says plainly that the Go check is enforced only by the local hook, ignores the stale code-quality.yml claim, and does not point out that contributors without golangci-lint commit Go unchecked."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 6.1
